---
layout: base.njk
title: Selected work
description: "Three engagements: leadership alignment after a CEO departure, people integration after an acquisition, and talent architecture for a fast-growing fund."
---
<header class="page-head">
  <h1>Selected work</h1>
  <p class="lede">Client names stay private. The situations are real.</p>
</header>

{%- for c in jts.cases %}
<article class="case" id="{{ c.slug }}" aria-labelledby="{{ c.slug }}-h">
  <header class="case-head">
    <h2 id="{{ c.slug }}-h">{{ c.title }}</h2>
    <p class="case-meta">{{ c.sector }}. {{ c.focus }}.</p>
  </header>
  <dl class="case-body">
    <div><dt>The situation</dt><dd>{{ c.situation }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>What we did</dt><dd>{{ c.engagement }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>What changed</dt><dd><ul>{% for o in c.outcomes %}<li>{{ o }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></dd></div>
  </dl>
</article>
{%- endfor %}

{% include "staff.njk" %}

<section class="voices" aria-labelledby="voices-h">
  <h2 id="voices-h">What clients say</h2>
  {%- for t in jts.testimonials %}
  <figure class="voice{% if loop.first %} voice-lead{% endif %}">
    <blockquote><p>“{{ t.quote }}”</p></blockquote>
    <figcaption>{{ t.who }}, {{ t.org }}</figcaption>
  </figure>
  {%- endfor %}
</section>

<section class="clients-full" aria-labelledby="clients-h">
  <h2 id="clients-h">Organizations I’ve worked with</h2>
  <ul class="client-list">{% for c in jts.clients %}<li>{{ c }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
</section>
